{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L96jvsuCmnv6Jg3C6hTYHK","type":"tool_result","content":"taskspec: unknown command 'initiative'\nTaskSpec — atomic contracts and native AI engineering toolkit\n\nUsage: taskspec [--json] [--dry-run] <command> [options]\n\n  init               creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\n  setup              none\n  demo               creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\n  example            writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\n  new                creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\n  plan               none\n  batch              creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\n  migrate            atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\n  validate           refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\n  dod                none\n  gate               executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\n  handoff            stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\n  run                runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\n  accept             executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\n  author-doctor      none\n  holdout            seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\n  receipt            creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\n  eval-audit         uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\n  identity           init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\n  evidence           run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\n  bridge             export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\n  dsse               export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\n  mcp                read-only stdio server\n  mesh               optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n  ready              none\n  graph              none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\n  status             none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n  lint               none\n  transition         changes lifecycle status and derived state\n  rebuild-state      rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\n  archive            moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\n  backup             writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\n  metrics            none\n  conformance        self-test uses disposable fixtures only\n  executor           reference L2 executor; transitions, executes, accepts, or parks one supplied task\n  agent-context      none\n  completion         none\n  doctor             none\n  version            none\n  help               none\n  decompose          Native intent decomposition, signed topology review, and TaskPlan compilation.\n  recipe             Inspect and validate resolved bounded execution guidance.\n  guide              Read version-matched installed workflow guidance.\n\nUse taskspec help <command>, taskspec guide <topic>, or taskspec agent-context.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4dc50d7-e867-44b9-8e2c-67008d4da482","uuid":"31a2d779-260b-4c23-bf7a-9db5c4c9d0b6","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:24:42.821Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"taskspec: unknown command 'initiative'\nTaskSpec — atomic contracts and native AI engineering toolkit\n\nUsage: taskspec [--json] [--dry-run] <command> [options]\n\n  init               creates missing tasks/ and .taskspec/config\n  setup              none\n  demo               creates and removes an isolated temporary repository\n  example            writes one installed canonical example non-clobberingly; --force replaces and --dry-run writes nothing\nExamples: task-plan, intent, recipe, incident, release-evidence. Use taskspec help example <kind>.\n  new                creates one Task-Spec scaffold and derived state\n  plan               none\n  batch              creates declared Task-Spec scaffolds; --dry-run writes nothing\n  migrate            atomically upgrades one explicitly named legacy task under the task-state lock\n  validate           refreshes deterministic derived state unless --no-state\n  dod                none\n  gate               executes task evals; --stamp additionally writes the sign-off envelope\n  handoff            stdout is read-only; --out writes non-clobberingly unless --force\n  run                runs declared eval commands in the task workspace\n  accept             executes acceptance evals; --stamp additionally writes AcceptanceRecord/v1 and the acceptance envelope\n  author-doctor      none\n  holdout            seal/run may write descriptor or receipt; verify is read-only\n  receipt            creator/sign commands write explicit receipt paths; validate is read-only\n  eval-audit         uses temporary git worktrees; optional report path\n  identity           init/sign/revoke write explicit files; verify is read-only\n  evidence           run writes an explicit evidence directory; validate/plan are read-only\n  bridge             export writes only with --out; validate is read-only\n  dsse               export writes only to --out; verify is read-only\n  mcp                read-only stdio server\n  mesh               optional repository-local control plane; run/cancel/resume/accept/finish/setup mutate disposable mesh state while canonical acceptance still calls Task-Spec\n  ready              none\n  graph              none; TaskGraphView/v1 is derived from Markdown and Git\n  status             none; emits TaskStatus/v1 and exactly one safe next command\n  lint               none\n  transition         changes lifecycle status and derived state\n  rebuild-state      rewrites deterministic tasks/_state.yaml\n  archive            moves root done/parked tasks under the task-state lock and refreshes derived state\n  backup             writes a timestamped backlog archive to the selected destination\n  metrics            none\n  conformance        self-test uses disposable fixtures only\n  executor           reference L2 executor; transitions, executes, accepts, or parks one supplied task\n  agent-context      none\n  completion         none\n  doctor             none\n  version            none\n  help               none\n  decompose          Native intent decomposition, signed topology review, and TaskPlan compilation.\n  recipe             Inspect and validate resolved bounded execution guidance.\n  guide              Read version-matched installed workflow guidance.\n\nUse taskspec help <command>, taskspec guide <topic>, or taskspec agent-context.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
