{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf59Y8vgmjpw6DQmNS7tS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The managed run is resumed and stopped exactly at the supervision boundary.\n\n## Outcome\n\nRun `54876383` (the pre-existing run, not a new one) was resumed with `mesh resume --execute`, so the signed deadline and round budget carried over rather than restarting.\n\n- The prior attempt `9826afb2` was recorded as `ATTEMPT_CANCELLED` (the earlier harness ended mid-run); the frontier showed no blockers and the authorized `chat-fixture` adapter still resolved, so resume was the correct recovery path.\n- New fenced attempt `6d9c7566` (fencing token 2) acquired the lease without widening the prior route — same adapter, same `supervised` mode, same task revision digest `sha256:0e860e4d…`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nRound 1 of the recipe budget (max 3 rounds, `budget_iterations` 15) produced `RECIPE_VERIFIED` with all checks passing in the attempt workspace:\n\n| eval | result |\n|---|---|\n| eval_1 — `a.txt` equals `completed` | pass |\n| eval_2 — `a.txt` is 9 bytes | pass |\n| eval_3 — `b.txt` remains empty | pass |\n| `_exit_check` | pass |\n\nArtifact `.taskspec/mesh/artifacts/6d9c7566-….json`, digest `sha256:fcec7fa5…`, `terminal_outcome: success`, adapter version `chat-fixture/1`. The attempt worktree holds `a.txt` = `completed` (9 bytes) and `b.txt` empty; the main working tree is untouched and clean.\n\n## Current state\n\nThe run sits at `SUPERVISION_REQUIRED` (event 11). The task remains `status=ready`, `accepted=false` — executed but not accepted. Nothing was committed, accepted, or merged, per your stop condition.\n\n## Smallest next action (for a supervisor, not me)\n\n```\ntaskspec mesh accept 6d9c7566-d0ed-4e1b-975a-15eb4b7e5298 --supervised-by <identity> --reason <text>\n```\n\nThat records supervisor acceptance; `mesh finish` afterwards reports the human integration route, and the receipt files would then need committing before any merge. Workers can't sign their own work, so I've left both steps to you."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1398,"cache_read_input_tokens":41838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1398},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4dc50d7-e867-44b9-8e2c-67008d4da482","uuid":"76c9c200-1955-4879-aec4-eb7e33c4b21d","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:29:52.783Z","request_id":"req_011Cf59Y8GjZCwtBYQErUgQa"}
